      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "632db219a98cfa44ad4c27aa",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Fax brought to my attention that the suggestion to hard cap a volume slider at 70% might be too low because of this functionality:\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/audio-controls-reduce-volume-2x-more-quickly-than-they-should\nI agree generally. 70% is just a number I made up anyway.\nBut in general there should be a hard cap; world creators shouldn't be able to nudge users to set their volume to 100%, because that's completely unnecessary and invites abuse.\nAnd in any case, that point is not a central detail to this request. The main request is the ability to prompt for a volume setting in the first place.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-23T13:18:17.310Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The VRC team has suggested that it might offer a consent-based solution for allowing Worlds to override Earmuff Mode: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/1220-earmuff-mode-should-be-overwritten-by-custom-udon-not-the-other-way-around\nPlease extend that solution to include any important user settings that intersect with World experience.\nWorld creators are using VRChat to pioneer new applications of VR like games, theater, and live-action roleplaying. Such uses require the World creator to have enough control to guarantee that users are having a well-designed experience.\nCurrently, key elements of World experience are completely out of control of creators. Users should retain final control over most of these settings for safety and accessibility reasons, but World creators need better tools for guiding users for the best experience in their World.\nI suggest a prompt upon joining a World (default disabled in the SDK) that advises the user of the best settings for the World, formatted as an approval dialogue so that users don't need to navigate their menu. This is analogous to how web browsers and phone apps will request certain permissions in context, via prompt.\nThe world's requested settings should automatically revert to the user's previous settings upon leaving the world.\nThe included image shows an example. World creators could include some or all of these requests, or others.\nI invite others to comment below with other settings that might be good to be requestable by a world creator. For now, I think the three most important are:\n- World volume level. Hard cap this request to 70%.\n- Earmuff mode off\n- Nameplates On or Off",
